{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966812,"nonce":"X3jVSPUfOzGpoB3sliMOMtExBiA=","title":"DSL mounts one Stateful at the view root, so @stateful on any component re-renders the","message":"**The defect.** `@stateful` on a component does not scope its rebuild.\n`detect_and_strip_stateful_views` folds every decorator into a program-level\n`has_stateful_view` flag, and `view_widget` then mounts a single `Stateful` at\nthe view root whose `on_state` calls `render_main`. Blinc core is correct --\n`Stateful` rebuilds its subtree -- but the DSL hands it the whole program as\nthat subtree. Every FSM transition re-renders everything, so any state keyed on\nnode identity (scroll offset, focus, CSS-created scroll physics) is destroyed.\n\n`set_rebuild` is NOT involved: it is never called anywhere in the DSL, runtime\nor cn layers, and DSL signal writes all go through `Signal::set`. The dirty flag\nis never raised. This is purely a mount-granularity problem.\n\n**The fix shape** (runtime half already exists):\n`blinc_runtime::view::render_component(renderer, name)` renders one component's\n`$view` symbol. A decorated component should mount its own `Stateful` at its\ncall site, with `on_state` calling that instead of `render_main`.\n\n**Attempt saved at** `scratchpad/scoped_stateful_wip.patch` (663 lines) plus\n`scratchpad/scoped_stateful.rs`. Reverted to keep the tree green. What it did:\n\n- `detect_stateful_components` -\u003e per-component `(name, deps, fsms)`, read\n  BEFORE markers are stripped; `saw_stateful` narrowed to the top-level view\n  only (`process(body, is_top_level)`).\n- `__blinc_stateful_component__` extern in `widget_ffi.rs`, registered in\n  `abi.rs` AND in the grammar symbol table (`blinc.zyn`) -- BOTH are required,\n  or lowering fails with \"Call to undefined function\" and the *enclosing* fn is\n  silently dropped, so the error names the caller, not the missing symbol.\n- `lower_component_calls` rewrites a prop-less stateful component call to that\n  extern.\n\n**Two obstacles hit, in order:**\n\n1. *JIT re-entrancy deadlock.* The extern runs inside a JIT call, which holds\n   `JitViewRenderer`'s `Arc\u003cMutex\u003cZyntaxRuntime\u003e\u003e`. `Stateful::on_state`\n   invokes its closure eagerly for the first render, and calling\n   `render_component` there re-locks the same runtime -\u003e self-deadlock.\n   Worked around by passing the call-site-rendered subtree in as an argument\n   and only re-entering the JIT on *subsequent* invocations.\n\n2. *SIGABRT, no diagnostic.* After the workaround, the JIT aborts. Most likely\n   the synthesized nested `\u003cName\u003e$view()` call never receives the leading\n   `__instance_id__: u64` that `inject_user_view_instance_id_params` adds to\n   every component view, because the paired `inject_call_site_keys` pass\n   probably does not descend into an extern call's arguments. Verify that\n   before anything else; the fix is likely to run the rewrite AFTER call-site\n   key injection, or to reuse the fully-lowered call node as the argument.\n\nProps are out of scope either way: `render_component` takes no arguments, so a\nre-render would drop them. The attempt only rewrote the prop-less shape.\n\nSee gotcha dsl view root viewport, feedback stateful container.","files":null}]}